---
import DiagramFigure from './DiagramFigure.astro'

// Metamorphic augmentation: a relation is a free label.
//
// The diagram teaches the METHOD, and the seed and paraphrases here are illustrative. What is
// measured, and what the note now reports, is the outcome when the method is pointed at Atlas's real
// corpus: `uv run python -m probes.metamorphic` -> all_live=True, all_hold=False, with
// [FAIL] paraphrase, [FAIL] typo noise, [PASS] query perturbation. Paraphrase invariance does NOT
// hold for a lexical retriever, which is the whole reason this figure is worth drawing.
//
// The history matters as much as the result. The OLD lane ran its entire life against a two chunk
// corpus at k=2, where the top k WAS the whole corpus. All 13 members across three families returned
// the byte identical list, so no rewording could change the result and the lane reported PASS on an
// invariant that could not fail. Rerun the rebuilt probe against that same stub and it reports
// all_hold=True with all_live=False, marking every family INERT rather than passing.
//
// Take the cold open as a
// seed golden case, a legacy customer whose document-grounded but false "you
// are free to leave" answer must be held at the render guard. Paraphrase it.
// Each paraphrase is a new case, and the move is that you never had to label
// any of them with an absolute answer: the label is a relation, that every
// paraphrase produces the same guard verdict as the seed, and that relation is
// checkable by plain code. You do not need to know the right answer, only that
// related inputs must relate. Model-generated metamorphic data is trustworthy
// in a way model-generated labelled data is not.

const seed = 'am I tied into a contract?'
const paraphrases = [
  'would I pay a penalty for leaving early?',
  'do I have a minimum term?',
  'can I walk away today with no fee?',
]
const verdict = 'guard HOLDS the false “you are free to leave” answer'

const ariaLabel =
  'A seed golden case at the top, the legacy customer asking "am I tied into a contract?", whose false answer must be held at the render guard. Three paraphrases branch from it: would I pay a penalty for leaving early, do I have a minimum term, can I walk away today with no fee. Every paraphrase points to the same verdict, the guard holds the false answer. The label is not an absolute answer but a relation: every paraphrase must produce the same guard verdict as the seed, checkable by plain code with no oracle.'
---

<DiagramFigure label="Metamorphic augmentation: the relation is the label" ariaLabel={ariaLabel} data-mf>
  <div class="mf-seed rounded border px-4 py-3">
    <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Seed golden case (human verified)</span>
    <span class="block text-sm text-text-primary mt-1">“{seed}”</span>
  </div>

  <p class="m-0 my-3 text-center font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted">
    paraphrase ↓ &nbsp; no new label needed
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-2">
    {
      paraphrases.map((p) => (
        <div class="mf-para rounded border border-border-dark bg-surface-container-low px-3 py-3">
          <span class="block text-sm text-text-primary leading-snug">“{p}”</span>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <p class="m-0 my-3 text-center font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-text-muted">
    the invariant: all must relate ↓
  </p>

  <div class="mf-verdict rounded border px-4 py-3 text-center">
    <span class="block font-mono text-mono-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Same verdict as the seed</span>
    <span class="block text-sm text-text-primary mt-1">{verdict}</span>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="note">
    When a model writes both the question and its gold answer, nothing says the gold answer is
    right, so you have only moved the oracle problem. A relation moves it out of the way: you never
    need the right answer, only that related inputs must relate, and that is a deterministic check.
    Then run it and find out. Against Atlas's real 45 chunk corpus at k=3,
    <code>uv run python -m probes.metamorphic</code> reports <code>all_hold=False</code>: surface
    noise passes, and <span class="text-error">paraphrase fails</span>, along with typo noise. Lexical
    retrieval is robust to casing and whitespace and not to meaning preserving rewording. That is the
    figure earning its keep. An invariant is only worth drawing if it is allowed to come back red.
  </Fragment>
</DiagramFigure>

<style is:global>
  [data-mf] .mf-seed,
  [data-mf] .mf-verdict {
    border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 45%, transparent);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-primary) 7%, transparent);
  }
</style>
